Infrastructure-as-Code repository (`{{ cloud_provider }}`) managed with Terraform.

## Structure

```
.
├── docs/                       # Documentation
├── iac/
│   └── ws-{{ workspace_name }}/   # Terraform working directory
│       ├── main.tf             # Root module composition
│       ├── terraform.tf        # Terraform settings, backend, required providers
│       ├── providers.tf        # Provider configuration
│       ├── variables.tf        # Input variables
│       ├── outputs.tf          # Output values
│       ├── locals.tf           # Local values
│       └── data.tf             # Data sources
├── modules/                    # Reusable child modules
├── scripts/                    # Helper scripts
└── .github/workflows/pipeline.yml  # CI/CD (plan on PR, apply on merge to main)
```

Additional workspaces can be added under `iac/` as `ws-<name>/`.

## Workflow

- Open a PR to `main` to run `terraform plan`.
- Merge to `main` to run `terraform apply`.

## Adding a workspace

Run the **Add Terraform Workspace** workflow (Actions tab → *Run workflow*)
and provide a workspace name. It scaffolds `iac/ws-<name>/` from the shared
template and opens a pull request with the new workspace.

## Updating from the template

This repo was scaffolded with [Copier](https://copier.readthedocs.io).
To pull later improvements from the template, run:

```
copier update
```
